# Rule 3 of the product direction (issue #3; docs/VIABLE.md, "What an act may move"): no jolts. A window moves once, to where
# it ends up.
# Story: an ordinary half hour with four windows. After every act, whatever Arbor moved it moved once.
# arbor-sim looks for this after every line of every scenario (MOVED TWICE); here each act also says so itself.
quiet
open Safari 900x600
open Terminal 600x400
open Mail 700x500
open Notes 400x300
move 104 1000 500 400 300
dock 101 left
expect moved-once
dock 102 right
expect moved-once
dock 103 beside 102 bottom
expect moved-once
# The view goes in, sideways, out and back.
zoom 101
expect moved-once
expect fills 101
neighbor right
expect moved-once
back
expect moved-once
out
expect moved-once
show-all
expect still
zoom 103
expect moved-once
out
expect moved-once
home
expect moved-once
# Sizes and places.
resize 101 right 60
expect moved-once
swap 102 103
expect moved-once
dock 103 left
expect moved-once
# Windows come and go.
minimize 102
expect moved-once
restore 102
expect moved-once
float 103
expect moved-once
expect size 103 700x500
close 102
expect moved-once
# All at once.
arrange
expect moved-once
float-all
expect moved-once
expect size 101 900x600
expect size 104 400x300
